    "summary": "Fiery Lovelight and tight China Cat jam in a short, punchy set",
    "blurb": "The band delivers a scorching Turn On Your Lovelight with Pigpen’s rap and Jerry’s smoking solo. The China Cat Sunflower > I Know You Rider segue is tight, highlighted by Phil’s strong bass lines, while High Time and Good Lovin’ keep the energy high throughout the brief set.",
    "review": "On December 13, 1969 at Swing Auditorium, the Dead rolled out an eleven‑song set that feels both compact and combustible. Highlights include a blazing Turn On Your Lovelight where Jerry’s guitar “smokes” and Pigpen throws one of his most spirited rap verses, plus a crisp, well‑balanced China Cat Sunflower > I Know You Rider jam powered by Phil’s great bass work. Even with the final portion of Black Peter cut, the performance stays engaging—High Time, Good Lovin’, and Cumberland Blues keep the momentum rolling, and Tom Constanten’s organ lick adds sparkle during the Lovelight break. Recorded from a clear soundboard source, the tape captures the band’s mid‑set jams with surprising fidelity for ’69, making this one of the more listenable early shows despite its brevity.",
